                    [ 'Light marble', 'Low; paint fill helps', 'Weak: the light surface reflects the beam', 'Subtle, matte mark', 'Test first' ],
                    [ 'River pebbles', 'Depends on colour; dark ones are better', 'Dark stones', 'Yes; watch the focus', 'Small stones; test first' ],
                    [ 'Glazed ceramic tiles', 'Depends on the glaze', 'Dark glazes; white ones poorly', 'Matte mark in the glaze', 'Fine detail in the glaze; test first' ],
                ] ],
                [ 'h2', 'Uneven and heavy stones: focus, camera and riser' ],
                [ 'p', 'A laser engraves sharply only within a narrow height range around the focal point. On a flat tile that is easy, but a pebble, a slate with a split edge or a garden stone has height differences that leave part of the mark blurred and weaker. A few rules:' ],
                [ 'ul', [
                    'Pick the flattest part of the stone and fit the design there – the smaller the graphic, the smaller the height difference beneath it.',
